<%# The wallet, as a pill in the corner of every account page.

    It is a LINK first and a hover surface second, which is the whole reason it
    can replace a tab: a tap opens the wallet, on a phone where there is no
    hover and on a keyboard where there is no pointer. The breakdown is a peek
    a mouse gets for free — nothing lives in it that the page it links to does
    not also say.

    Drawn only when something has been collected. A "0" pill would be an
    affordance promising a screen whose whole content is "no points yet", and
    the wallet already made the choice not to show a zero.

    It renders into the layout's fixed top corner rather than where it is
    called, because that corner is where the language switcher already is and
    the two have to share one cluster. So the partial fills `:top_corner` and
    emits nothing itself — call it anywhere in the page body.

    Locals: rows (every Verto with a pile, newest first), total, current. %>
<% content_for :top_corner do %>
<% if rows.any? %>
  <div class="you-purse" data-controller="wallet-pill"
       data-action="mouseenter->wallet-pill#open mouseleave->wallet-pill#close">
    <%= link_to you_wallet_path,
          class: "you-purse-pill#{" is-on" if current == :wallet}",
          "aria-label": t("you.wallet_pill", total: number_with_delimiter(total)),
          "aria-current": (current == :wallet ? "page" : nil),
          data: { action: "focus->wallet-pill#open blur->wallet-pill#close" } do %>
      <%# A wallet, not a coin: each Verto sets its own token icons, so borrowing
          one of them to stand for the total would say that all of it is that
          Verto's currency. (A stack of coins was the first try and read as a
          database cylinder at 15px.) %>
      <svg class="you-purse-mark" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect x="1.6" y="3.4" width="12.8" height="9.2" rx="2.4"
              stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <path d="M14.4 6.7h-2.5a1.85 1.85 0 0 0 0 3.7h2.5"
              stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
      <span class="you-purse-total"><%= number_with_delimiter(total) %></span>
    <% end %>

    <%# aria-hidden, and not as a shortcut: the pill's own label carries the
        total, and every row in here is on the wallet page the pill points at,
        so a screen reader following the pill loses nothing. Exposing it would
        put the same five Vertos in the reading order of every account page.
        The link inside is tabindex=-1 for the same reason — and because
        focusable content inside aria-hidden is a trap rather than a shortcut. %>
    <div class="you-purse-popover" data-wallet-pill-target="popover" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
      <div class="you-purse-head"><%= t("you.wallet_eyebrow") %></div>
      <% rows.first(YouController::PURSE_PREVIEW).each do |row| %>
        <div class="you-purse-row">
          <div class="you-purse-verto"><%= row[:survey].theme.presence || row[:survey].title %></div>
          <%# That Verto's own tokens, named and counted the way that Verto names
              and counts them. Two Vertos routinely both call a token "gold" for
              two different things, so the piles are never added together — not
              here, and not on the page this links to. %>
          <div class="you-purse-piles">
            <% row[:piles].each do |pile| %>
              <span class="you-pile">
                <%= pile[:icon] %> <b><%= number_with_delimiter(pile[:amount]) %></b> <%= pile[:name] %>
              </span>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <%= link_to you_wallet_path, class: "you-purse-all", tabindex: -1 do %>
        <%= t("you.wallet_see_all") %> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
<% end %>
